to-be-incorporated-into-paper-lines-84 = cons "" (cons "A shared subterm is held by a duplicating cell that copies lazily, one level at a time as it is" (cons "read. A stored value lives once, and readers copy its top cell. A substitution of dimensions is" (cons "recorded on the reference, not applied by copying. A subterm in a position that might not be read" (cons "is held unbuilt until an operation meets it: `fst (a , b)` never computes `b`, even if `b`" (cons "diverges. `delay e` holds `e` so wherever it stands: it has `e`'s type, an operation meeting it" (cons "builds it, `force` of it is it, and its code is `cthunk` (the first-order and C++ back ends," (cons "being strict, compute it where it stands). A λ's subterms that do not mention its variable are computed once, however often the λ is" (cons "applied. A case is one cell, and selecting a branch is one step." (cons "" (cons "Equal terms reached by different routes are also computed once. Every cell that will produce a" (cons "value (a thunk, a saturated call, an application of a known λ, a case) carries a key: its compiled" (cons "body over the keys of the values bound in it, interned, so one term is one pointer. A value's key" (cons "is its constructor over its parts' keys; a held value (a box) is named by what was put in it, and a" (cons "copy out of a box, a definition unfolded, and the scrutinee a case branch rebuilds from the fields" (cons "it took all carry that name, so one value has one name by whatever route it is reached. A producer" (cons "is pending on its key from its creation; when one fires while another of the same key is pending," (cons "its value goes into a box held by the entry, and the other reads the box instead of computing" (cons "(waiting on the wire, uncounted, if the value has not arrived). Retention is reachability: an" (cons "entry lives exactly while a producer is pending or a reader holds the box; the table holds nothing" (cons "on its own, and two boxes with equal values but different origins are not identified (a numeral" (cons "computed by `add` and the same numeral written out are two values). Naive Fibonacci shows it:" (cons "`fib (n+2)` demands `fib (n+1)`, which demands `fib n` while the outer `fib n`" (cons "is pending, so every `fib k` is computed once and the work is linear in the calls (unary addition" (cons "dominates the count), whether the argument is a numeral the machine computed or one written out." (cons "" (cons "Compiled code follows the same rule. Records (a λ's or thunk's body) and case tables are interned," (cons "so equal code compiled twice is one pointer, and the checker compiles every definition's quoted" (cons "code again at each reading. Between top-level forms the code is sorted by what still refers to it:" (cons "what a definition, a cell or kept code can build from is kept whole; what only keys name (a λ's" (cons "key is its record over its captures' keys) loses its body and keeps the hash and SHA-256 interning" (cons "compares, so equal code compiled later gets the same pointer and the body back, and the memo finds" (cons "what it found before; the rest is freed. Output and step counts are those of keeping everything" (cons "(`CUBICAL_NOSWEEP=1`); `CUBICAL_SWEEPALL=1` sorts after every form, `CUBICAL_MEMEND=1` reports" (cons "the split at exit." (cons "" (cons "A reading reports its steps, and with them the memo hits (values found instead of computed) and" (cons "the values shared. The steps are the work this reading did, given what earlier readings left held" (cons "and the order the rewrites ran in: a term's second reading can cost less than its first, and with" (cons "workers a reading can find a value shared that it would have computed alone. Without the memo" (cons "(`CUBICAL_NOMEMO=1`) the count is a property of the term, the same at any number of workers;" (cons "with the memo the answers are." nil)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
